        "eyebrow": "Our vision",
        "body": "<h2>Planted Here. Sent Everywhere.</h2>\n<p>Planted in culturally diverse St. Louis. Sent to the world as a congregation alive to the Gospel that breaks every wall — welcoming every person, bearing bold witness to the saving grace of God through Jesus, from our neighborhood to the nations.</p>\n<p>Timothy Lutheran Church is a congregation alive to the Gospel of Jesus Christ. Gathered in worship around the Word and Sacraments of the risen Lord, we accept every person as one for whom Christ died. Growing in faith through Christian education and honest community, we go — from our neighborhood to the nations — bearing the tangible love of God to all.</p>\n<p>We are a congregation of the Lutheran Church — Missouri Synod (LCMS), rooted in the Lindenwood Park neighborhood of St. Louis.</p>\n<p>Gathering as God's people, celebrating His grace, receiving His gifts of Word and Sacrament.</p>\n<p>Intentionally welcoming and loving all people as Jesus does.</p>\n<p>Equipping people for a lifelong journey with Christ.</p>\n<p>Sharing the love of Jesus with those who don't yet know Him.</p>",
