        "subtitle": "",
        "eyebrow": "A unique — but familiar — sound",
        "body": "<p>We are a congregation shaped by the Lutheran liturgical tradition — and deeply open to the full range of musical gifts God has placed in our community. On any given Sunday you might hear a pipe organ prelude, a handbell choir, a drum kit, a hammer dulcimer, a steel drum ensemble, or an African choir. Sometimes all in the same service.</p>\n<p>The music here is wide-ranging because the grace we celebrate is wide-ranging. <em>A unique — but familiar — worship experience.</em></p>",
